        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart: The old cup",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kopf originally meant a cup or bowl. It is related to English cup; both were early borrowings of Late Latin cuppa. A container word became slang for the skull and eventually took over the everyday job."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "German’s older inherited head-word did not disappear completely. The next micro-lesson follows it into compounds and compares the same container metaphor in French."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
