    {
      "id": "GE-C17-kopf-haupt",
      "sequence": 670,
      "title": "Kopf / Haupt — two head-words",
      "headword": "Kopf / Haupt",
      "romanization": "Kopf / Haupt",
      "gloss": "the cup-word and the inherited Germanic head-word",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:8003a50624d2c393",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Kopf began as “cup.” German’s inherited word for “head” is Haupt, a cousin of English head and Latin caput."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart: inherited Haupt",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "language",
                "inherited form"
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 3,
              "utterances": [
                "language: Latin. inherited form: caput.",
                "language: German. inherited form: Haupt.",
                "language: English. inherited form: head."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The initial k becomes h relationship reflects Grimm’s law, the same systematic Germanic sound shift seen in Latin pater beside English father. The later consonants have their own history; use the initial pair as the clear signal."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Haupt survives in compounds and formal vocabulary:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hauptstadt — capital, literally “head city”;"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hauptbahnhof — main station;"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Hauptsache — main thing."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "“Kopf — everyday cup-word”",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: “Kopf — everyday cup-word”]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "“Haupt — inherited head-word”",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: “Haupt — inherited head-word”]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "“Hauptstadt, Hauptbahnhof”",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: “Hauptstadt, Hauptbahnhof”]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "“Kopf took the job; Haupt stayed in compounds.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which word is everyday “head”? (Kopf.) Which inherited word survives in compounds? (Haupt.) Name two compounds. (Hauptstadt, Hauptbahnhof.) What parallel metaphor did French use? (Tête, originally a pot.) Next: the hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "GE-C17-kopf-haupt-compound-word",
              "prompt": "Which inherited German head-word survives in compounds such as Hauptstadt?",
              "assesses": [
