      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:7f67569d5e4ed938",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before going on: say die Hand again, and what it means."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way: Where the family tree stops",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now the interesting part. Every Romance language builds \"hand\" on Latin manus:"
            },
            {
              "kind": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                ""
              ],
              "columns": 2,
              "rowCount": 4,
              "utterances": [
                "French, la main.",
                "Italian, la mano.",
                "Portuguese, a mão.",
                "Spanish, la mano."
              ]
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And Germanic — German, English — has handuz, which is not related to manus at all. The two families simply have different words here."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That is worth noticing, because these connections keep turning up, and it can start to feel as though everything must connect. It doesn't. Indo-European languages share a great deal, and then diverge, and \"hand\" is one of the places where they diverged early and completely."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The Latin word did reach German — but only as borrowed vocabulary: Manuskript, Maniküre, manuell. Learned imports, sitting beside the native word without displacing it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what this lesson added to die Hand, in one sentence",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: what this lesson added to **die Hand**, in one sentence]"
            }
